{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4325474,"ns":0,"title":"Geometric analysis","extract":"Geometric analysis is a mathematical discipline where tools from differential equations, especially elliptic partial differential equations (PDEs), are used to establish new results in differential geometry and differential topology. The use of linear elliptic PDEs dates at least as far back as Hodge theory.","description":"Field of higher mathematics","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}